    challengesLabel: THE CHALLENGES
    challenge: <p data-start="232" data-end="465"><strong data-start="232" data-end="252">Donor management</strong><br data-start="252" data-end="255">Without a dedicated CRM, donor history is scattered across spreadsheets and inboxes. Segmenting donors, personalizing follow-ups, or identifying strategic donors before it is too late becomes nearly impossible.</p><p data-start="467" data-end="699"><strong data-start="467" data-end="494">Fundraising &amp; campaigns</strong><br data-start="494" data-end="497">Coordinating multichannel fundraising campaigns — email, website, events — without an integrated tool leads to duplicates, inconsistent data, and a loss of traceability that damages donor relationships.</p><p data-start="701" data-end="931"><strong data-start="701" data-end="721">Grant management</strong><br data-start="721" data-end="724">Each funder has its own conditions, payment schedules, and reporting formats. Managing several grants simultaneously without a dedicated tool exposes the organization to compliance errors and funding delays.</p><p data-start="933" data-end="1137"><strong data-start="933" data-end="956">Fund usage tracking</strong><br data-start="956" data-end="959">Proving to funders that every euro is spent in line with grant objectives requires rigorous project-based analytical accounting. Without it, every audit becomes a risky exercise.</p><p data-start="1139" data-end="1356"><strong data-start="1139" data-end="1172">Impact statistics &amp; reporting</strong><br data-start="1172" data-end="1175">International donors and funders require accurate impact reports. Manually consolidating field data scattered across different countries takes weeks and produces unreliable reports.</p>
